I will remove aggregates and special territories as needed, and standardize names. Then sort alphabetically.

```python
cands = ['Algeria','Bahrain','Brunei Darussalam','China','Gabon','Luxembourg','Macao SAR, China','Malaysia','Oman','Qatar','Saudi Arabia','Singapore']
filtered = []
for c in cands:
    if '(' in c:
        continue
    if c == 'Macao SAR, China':
        continue  # exclude SARs for this task
    if c == 'Brunei Darussalam':
        filtered.append('Brunei')
    else:
        filtered.append(c)
print(', '.join(sorted(filtered)))
